# Localization
@scenario tutorial_lesson_14
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip guide neutral]
pip: Use a localization key to display a line in the selected language.
pip: i18n:tutorial.greeting
pip: That line uses tutorial.greeting in config/locales/en.properties. Edit its value and replay.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
pip: What should stay the same when you rewrite a translation?
> Every character of the translated sentence. -> retry
> Its lookup key. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show pip guide curious]
pip: Stable keys let the same scene select a different localized line. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip guide cheer]
pip: Stable keys let the same scene select a different localized line.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_14]
[flag tutorial_done_14]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_4]
